{{#extend "layout"}}

  {{#content "main"}}
  <section class="hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Your choices</p>
    <h1>Cookies</h1>
    <p>
      A cookie is a small file a website keeps in your browser. Some make this site work and
      are always on. The rest are set only if you allow them: a visit counter of our own,
      Google Tag Manager, and YouTube when you play a video.
    </p>
    <p>
      You can change your choice at any time with <em>Cookie settings</em>, at the foot of
      every page. Switching a kind of cookie off deletes the ones this site set; cookies
      that Google or YouTube set on their own sites stay until you clear them in your
      browser.
    </p>
  </section>

  {{!-- Made from config.consent, so it lists exactly what the banner asks
        about. On a narrow screen each table scrolls sideways in its own
        focusable region. --}}
  <div class="card">
    {{consentTable}}
  </div>
  {{/content}}

{{/extend}}
